# Solidity sources must compile to the same bytes on every OS.
# solc embeds keccak256 of each source file in the CBOR metadata at the end of the bytecode, so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true (CRLF) builds different bytecode than Linux/CI (LF): Blockscout then
# rejects or only partially matches the LF standard-JSON inputs ThaiXTrade submits for factory tokens.
*.sol text eol=lf
